snippet.textDisplay:
@PanzerIVAEit’s about the distribution of the population, not the size of the land. US population is spread out wide and far, whereas China’s population is highly concentrated to smaller areas. So high speed rails are much more practical in China. It’s a low priority on America because it’s not needed. 
Also, in China  the government owns all the land so they can just build wherever and wherever they want. This is not true in USA, Europe or Japan. This is also one of the reasons it takes much longer time to build high speed rails in Japan and Europe than in China. Also, there are environmental issues and laws on the other places that China does not have

Edit - I wrote “on” a couple of times. It should be “in” Just a typo

